	)
	(text_box "Drivetrain, Arm, and Science all use the same subsystem power control and monitoring architecture. \nEach subsystem is gated by an AND gate always dependent on the ESTOP NC condition, and the respective GPIO that enables each subsystem. After the AND gate, a gate drive with Inrush control and OVLO config, drives the N-Channel Mosfet to the load.\nGiven the inductive properties of each load, a schottky diode is placed at each LT7001 gate driver as a freewheeling diode.\nAs the inductive load (motor driver + motor) can be shut off abrubtly depending on the condition, and inductive load can recycle current back to its source for a bried period of time. A schottky diode prevents damaging the gate driver bst and ts pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 144.145 27.305 0)
		(size 53.975 50.165)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "93a90f6a-a703-4972-8250-895b926df798")
	)
